  "description": "Given a sorted array `nums`, remove the duplicates in-place such that each unique element appears only once. The relative order of the elements should be kept the same. Return the new length. You must do this by modifying the input array in-place with O(1) extra memory.",
  "pseudocode": "function removeDuplicates(nums):\n1     if nums.length == 0:\n2         return 0\n3     \n4     slow = 0 // Pointer for the next unique element position\n5     for fast from 1 to nums.length - 1: // Pointer to iterate through the array\n6         if nums[fast] != nums[slow]: // If a new unique element is found\n7             slow = slow + 1 // Move slow pointer forward\n8             nums[slow] = nums[fast] // Place the unique element at slow's position\n9     return slow + 1 // The new length is slow + 1 (0-indexed to 1-indexed count)",
